                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "\"Lame\" would be the best word to describe this apology for a game. Lame, lazy storytelling. Lame, cringey dialogues and characters that make you wonder what the hell the authors were smoking. No voiceovers, except for the opening and the final scenes. The puzzle \"difficulty\" is a joke (putting together an eight-piece letter, picking up the only collectible item and using it on the only active hotspot in the room, etc.). 95% of the time you're just running back and forth to perform one mundane task after another. The only good thing about this piece of... ahem, gamedev is that I managed to beat it in one sitting in under two hours—otherwise, I wouldn't have tolerated this nonsense any longer. Even if you're the most avid fan of good old point-and-click adventures from the 2000s, don't let your nostalgia get the better of you and just give this one a hard pass. Can't recommend purchasing it even at a discount.",
